{
  "abstract": "Let $C$ be the cyclic sixth-root cover of the projective line with eight branch points of multiplicities (2,2,2,2,1,1,1,1), and let $H$ be its primitive Eisenstein Hodge structure of rank six over $K=\\mathbf Q(\\zeta_3)$. We prove that, on a nonempty Zariski-open set of ordered configurations, the middle exterior cube of $H$ after two fixed CM twists has codimension-two support in degree five of the natural product of five curves. This rank-40 block has Hodge types $(3,2)$ and $(2,3)$, and its support is the first middle-exterior-power case beyond the seven-point construction. The elliptic carrier is birational to an explicit family of cubic threefolds. The associated fixed-parameter fourfolds are rationally connected; their odd fourth intersection cohomology is Tate. We prove the latter statement using a complete local Newton-face certificate after quadratic coordinate changes, a corrected Hodge-ideal comparison through the Milnor algebra, and an injective global first-jet map. Rational Hodge classes on the resolved fourfolds are algebraic by the uniruled-fourfold theorem. Relative Hilbert schemes then provide actual surface families, whose cylinder images give the required support. A common-open comparison controls all exceptional and vertical boundary contributions. Exact CPU computations and portable checkers accompany the proof. The result concerns this selected block on a configuration open; it does not assert an all-configuration or full Clifford correspondence theorem. The general rational Hodge conjecture remains open.",
